<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_2_1" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_2_1">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_2_1" name="3.2.1 Reagent Management" processRef="Process_L3_3_2_1"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_2_1" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L3/L0 Process. Chemical reagents are the primary selectivity control mechanism in flotation. Collectors attach to target mineral surfaces; frothers stabilise bubble-particle aggregates in the froth; depressants prevent non-target minerals from floating; pH modifiers (lime) control pulp chemistry to enable selective activation and depression.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_2_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_chem" name="Plant Chemist / Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_2_1_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_dcs" name="DCS Auto-control / Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_2_1_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_2_1_s" name="Shift start or reagent low-level alert">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1" name="3.2.1.1 Manage Reagent Inventory and Preparation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reagents are received from suppliers in bulk tanks, drums, or bags, inventoried in the ERP, and prepared (diluted to working concentration where required) in the reagent mixing area. Reagent usage is tracked by tank level change (mass = volume × density) per shift. Reagent consumption is a key variable cost and a P754-relevant input to mass balance integrity checks. [P754: mass (reagent consumption) | tank level sensor + density measurement | shift-end reconciliation | Principle 1 (mass of reagent inputs to mass balance) | NO]
ISA-95 level: 3
Actors: Plant Chemist; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Level 3; AMIRA P754 Principle 1
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (reagent_consumption_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2" name="3.2.1.2 Adjust Pulp pH with Lime">
      <bpmn:documentation>Quicklime or hydrated lime is added to the grinding circuit or flotation feed conditioning tank to achieve the target pH for the flotation circuit. At Cu-only circuits (QB, HVC), pH is typically maintained at 10–11.5 to depress pyrite. At sequential Cu-Zn circuits (Antamina), Cu flotation operates at elevated pH while Zn activation requires a lower pH adjustment after Cu concentrate removal. DCS controls lime dosing pump speed based on continuous inline pH measurement. [P754: mass (lime) + grade (pH as process parameter) | lime slurry flow meter + inline pH sensor | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2 | NO]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: pH_telemetry, lime_dosing_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3" name="3.2.1.3 Dose Collector, Frother, and Depressant">
      <bpmn:documentation>Dosing pumps inject collectors (xanthates, dithiophosphates for Cu/Zn; xanthates for Pb), frothers (MIBC, DF250), and depressants (sodium cyanide or zinc sulphate for Zn depression in Cu circuit; sodium silicate for gangue depression) into the flotation feed or individual flotation banks at metered flow rates. Dosage rates are controlled by DCS (flow rate setpoints from metallurgist) and logged continuously to PI Historian. [P754: mass (reagent) | positive displacement dosing pump flow meter | continuous (1-min) | Principles 1, 2 | NO — internal reagent input]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS Auto-control; Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 2
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: reagent_dosing_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_2_1_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_2_1_e" name="Feed conditioned at target pH">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_2_1_4</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_2_1_s" targetRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_2" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_3" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3" targetRef="End_L3_3_2_1_e"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_2_1">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_2_1" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_2_1">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_2_1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="916" height="340"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_chem_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_2_1_chem" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="876" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_2_1_dcs_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_2_1_dcs" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="190" width="876" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L3_3_2_1_s_di" bpmnElement="Start_L3_3_2_1_s"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="77" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="139" width="100" height="56"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_1"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_2"><dc:Bounds x="408" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_2_1_3_2_1_3"><dc:Bounds x="614" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_2_1_e_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_2_1_e"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="247" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="798" y="309" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_1"><di:waypoint x="166" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_2"><di:waypoint x="372" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="390" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="390" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="408" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_3"><di:waypoint x="578" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="614" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_2_1_4"><di:waypoint x="784" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="820" y="275"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
